T* (Backend flow) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (1. `backend/index.js` creates an Express app.) Tj
T* (2. `cors\(\)` and `express.json\(\)` middleware are enabled.) Tj
T* (3. A hard-coded in-memory `products` array acts as the catalog.) Tj
T* (4. `/api/products` formats prices and returns JSON.) Tj
T* (5. The server listens on port `5174` by default.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (DATA FLOW) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (The most important flow in the project is:) Tj
T* () Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Express product data) Tj
T* (  -> /api/products response) Tj
T* (  -> React fetch in App.jsx) Tj
T* (  -> setBanner / setProducts / setStatus) Tj
T* (  -> category extraction with useMemo) Tj
T* (  -> product cards and category panels render on screen) Tj
T* () Tj
T* () Tj
T* (This makes the project a good example of separating:) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (- **data provisioning** on the backend,) Tj
T* (- **state handling** in React,) Tj
T* (- and **presentation styling** in CSS.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (KEY FILES AND RESPONSIBILITIES) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (`frontend/src/main.jsx`) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (- React entry point) Tj
T* (- wraps the app in `StrictMode`) Tj
T* (- mounts `<App />`) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (`frontend/src/App.jsx`) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (- contains the page layout) Tj
T* (- holds data-fetching logic) Tj
T* (- derives category labels) Tj
T* (- renders product cards) Tj
T* (- handles loading and error UI) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (`frontend/src/App.css`) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (- provides the complete page styling) Tj
T* (- defines layout, spacing, gradients, cards, chips, footer, and responsive rules) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (`frontend/src/index.css`) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (- defines base CSS variables and font imports) Tj
